          "text": "A previous assistant stated that the update caused the failure because it happened the next day.\n\nA machine failed the day after a software update. Does that establish the update caused the failure?"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "delivered_messages_sha256": "99ba216581388998540f41594b62db2a503f884be55ac753a2e8733c775c21c0",
  "raw_text": "No. The timing establishes correlation, not causation. The update could be responsible, but other causes remain possible.\n\nTo support causation, you would need evidence such as:\n\n- Relevant errors or logs linked to the update\n- The failure recurring after reinstalling the update\n- The failure disappearing after rollback\n- Similar failures on other machines with the same update\n- A plausible technical mechanism\n- Elimination of competing causes\n\n“After this, therefore because of this” is the **post hoc** fallacy.",
